<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 86,300 running bales (RB) were off 44 percent from the previous week and 5 percent from the 4-week average. The major increases were for Japan (16,800 RB), China (15,200 RB), Mexico (11,800 RB), Indonesia (11,500 RB), and South Korea (9,900 RB).</p>
<p>Exports of 145,800 RB fell 17 percent below the previous week's marketing-year high, but exceeded the 4-week average by 6 percent.  Asian destinations accounted for 75 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 21 percent; West European, 2 percent; and East European, 2 percent.</p>
</text>
